# UI conventions

## Stylesheet load order

1. `static/css/common.css` — base resets and shared components
2. Page or module CSS (`dashboard.css`, `radio_modules.css`, or module `static/*.css`)
3. `constellation.css` — only on dashboard / pages using constellation background
4. `theme-dark-final.css` — **injected last by `common.js`** (do not link manually); dark cascade safety net

Use `url_for('static', filename='css/...')` with cache-bust `?v=X.X`.

## Dark mode (required)

- Every standalone page must load `static/js/common.js` (theme toggle + injects `theme-dark-final.css`).
- Module CSS that hardcodes `#fff` / `#2c3e50` must add `body.dark-mode…` overrides (see `docs/FRONTEND_THEME.md`).
- Before shipping a new module: `python scripts/audit_dark_mode.py --strict`
- Do **not** add `body.dark-mode span { color: … !important }` — it flattens chips/pills to one ink color.

## Dashboard

- Body class: `has-constellation-bg`
- Canvas: `#primenet-bg-canvas` driven by `constellation.js`
- Module cards in constellation deck — edit section blocks, not the whole 1800-line file

## Radio modules

- Extend behavior from `templates/radio_module.html` pattern: topbar, filters, `data-*` attrs on `<body>`
- Shared JS: `static/js/common.js` (`logout()`, shared helpers)

## Module templates

- Standalone modules (e.g. network health) keep their own layout but should share `common.css` and header link back to dashboard
- Prefer CSS classes over inline `style=""` attributes
- Bump `?v=` only on files you change

## Do not

- Copy-paste entire `<head>` blocks — match existing link tags and class naming in sibling templates
- Edit `modules/parameter_dictionary/huawei_params/` HTML
